-finally is a block that always runs after try-catch,
whether an exception happens or not.
-✅ When is finally executed?

 👉 In almost all cases:

 ✔ Exception occurs → runs
 ✔ No exception → runs
 ✔ Return statement → still runs
 ❌ Only NOT executed when:
 System crash
 System.exit() is called

 🎯 Where do we use finally?
 👉 Used for cleanup work, like:
 Closing file
 Closing database connection
 Releasing resources

 -finally always runs (no matter what happens).
 -Used to clean resources (file, DB, network).
 -Runs even if return statement is inside try/catch.
 -Helps avoid memory/resource leaks.
 -Comes after try and catch block.
 -You can use try + finally (without catch also).
 -If JVM stops (System.exit()), then finally will NOT run.

👉 finally will NOT execute when:
System.exit() is called
JVM is forcefully stopped (halt())
Infinite loop (control never reaches finally)
System crash / power failure

⚠️ Important Warning (Interview + Real life)
👉 Using return in finally is BAD practice
Because:
It hides original return value
It can hide exceptions